# First-party analytics proxy. Both lines must precede the SPA fallback, or
# /index.html swallows them.
#
# Why proxy instead of loading the script cross-origin: self-hosting alone does
# not beat uBlock Origin or Brave, because their filter lists match the
# /script.js path, not just the hostname. The upstream image is prebuilt, and
# TRACKER_SCRIPT_NAME is baked in at build time, so the renamed script is not
# served upstream and /site-utils.js 404s there. Proxying solves both: the
# browser only ever sees a same-origin request to an innocuous path, and the
# upstream host never appears in the page at all.
#
# The tracker derives its collect URL from its own script src directory, so a
# script served at /site-utils.js posts to /api/su on this same origin, which
# the second rule forwards. Renaming one without the other breaks collection.
/site-utils.js  https://assets.aralostudio.com/script.js  200
/api/su         https://assets.aralostudio.com/api/su     200

# SPA fallback — every other path serves index.html so client-side routing works.
/*  /index.html  200
